From: chainonyourdoor <chainonyourdoor@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 10:32:03 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] block: add ADIOS I/O scheduler v3.2.0 backport for android14-6.1

Backport of ADIOS (Adaptive Deadline I/O Scheduler) v3.2.0
by Masahito S <firelzrd@gmail.com> to android14-6.1 (Linux 6.1.x).

Original source: https://github.com/firelzrd/adios
Original patch:  linux6.12.44-ADIOS-3.2.0.patch

Backport changes for android14-6.1 compatibility:
- Adapted elevator.c to use elevator_get() instead of elevator_find_get()
  (elevator_find_get() does not exist in Linux 6.1)
- Preserved mq-deadline as default scheduler when ADIOS default is not
  selected (this tree has no SSG scheduler — an earlier version of this
  backport assumed SSG was the android14-6.1 default, which does not hold
  for chainonyourdoor/android_kernel_common-6.1; confirmed via direct read
  of block/elevator.c and grep across block/ turning up no ssg references
  at all, plus a real `patch --dry-run` failing on exactly this line)
- Fixed NULL pointer dereference in adios_completed_request() for UFS MCQ
  (rq->elv.priv[0] can be NULL for requests not going through elevator insert)
- Verified all blk-mq APIs are fully compatible with Linux 6.1.x

ADIOS overview:
ADIOS replaces the traditional deadline-based I/O scheduling with an
adaptive model that learns from historical I/O completion times. It
maintains 4 dispatch tiers (emergency, persistence, sync, async) and
dynamically adjusts per-request deadlines based on observed latency,
resulting in lower and more consistent I/O latency under mixed workloads.

Changes:
- block/adios.c        : new file — full ADIOS scheduler implementation
  including adaptive latency model, 4-tier priority dispatch, per-request
  deadline tracking, and sysfs tunables
- block/Kconfig.iosched : add MQ_IOSCHED_ADIOS and MQ_IOSCHED_DEFAULT_ADIOS
  config entries
- block/Makefile        : add adios.o build target
- block/elevator.c      : hook ADIOS as optional default scheduler via
  CONFIG_MQ_IOSCHED_DEFAULT_ADIOS, adapted for 6.1 elevator_get() API

Signed-off-by: chainonyourdoor <chainonyourdoor@gmail.com>
